ps://www.labri.fr/perso/sopena/pmwiki/uploads/Publications/TALK_Sopena_CID2019.pdf)\nciteturn8search17 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7.1 years ago; Theorem (Mácajová, Raspaud, Škoviera, 2016+).\nFor every signed graph (G,σ), χ±(G,σ) ≤ Δ(G), unless (G,σ) is an all-positive complete graph, an all-positive odd cycle, or an all-negative even cycle. ... This conjecture has been disproved by Kardoš and Narboni (2019+).\nχ of signed graphs – 2. via vertex colourings\n\nA Brooks-type Theorem\n\nTheorem (Mácajová, Raspaud, Škoviera, 2016+).\nFor every signed graph (G,σ), χ±(G,σ) ≤ Δ(G), unless (G,σ) is an all-positive complete graph, an all-positive odd cycle, or an all-negative even cycle.\nAlso, if G is k-degenerate, then χ±(G,σ) ≤ k + 1.\n\nPlanar graphs\n\nTheorem (Mácajová, Raspaud, Škoviera, 2016+).\nFor every signed planar graph (G,σ), χ±(G,σ) ≤ 5.\nMoreover, χ±(G,σ) ≤ 4 if g(G) ≥ 4, and χ±(G,σ) ≤ 3 if g(G) ≥ 5.\n\nThey also conjectured that χ±(G,σ) ≤ 4 for every signed planar graph (G,σ).\nThis conjecture has been disproved by Kardoš and Narboni (2019+).\n\nEric Sopena – CID 2019\n\n64--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\narXiv Troller (https://arxiv-troller.com/?q=paper%3A+2610.28030)\nciteturn8search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Counterexamples to the local antimagic leaf conjecture\n\nCounterexamples to the local antimagic leaf conjecture\n\nAndré Ebling Brondani, Francisca Andrea Macedo França\n\narXiv:2610.22783\n\nAuthors: André Ebling Brondani, Francisca Andrea Macedo França\n\nSubmitted: Oct 2026 | Updated: Oct 2026\n\nIt has been conjectured that $χ_{\\mathrm{la}}(T)\\leq\\ell(T)+2$ for every tree $T$ of order at least three, where $χ_{\\mathrm{la}}(T)$ is the local antimagic chromatic number and $\\ell(T)$ denotes the number of leaves. We disprove this bound and show that no absolute constant can replace $2$ in an inequality of this form. Our approach uses degree-based intervals containing all possible 